    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1108">

                <pb facs="0804" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/4313.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Letcher.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 17. This Department has advised Americans to withdraw from and remain
                    out of Mexico for the time being, and has felt that American interests employing
                    American workmen in that country would consider the lives of their employees of
                    first concern. But the Department has announced the self-evident fact that it
                    does not attempt to compel any American citizen to leave or to remain out of
                    that country. Those who contemplate remaining in Mexico or returning thereto
                    must know the risk they assume in so doing and the difficulties of securing or
                    affording to them adequate and timely protection by this Government. Individuals
                    must judge for themselves whether the proofs of protection by the authorities
                    are acceptable, and whether the conditions existing will justify them in
                    returning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
